        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47647?u=2fbfc431a85d357f00c0146d5e55b425b7f00a3d&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Chrome and Edge 148 desktop have added support for <a href=\"https://www.w3.org/TR/appmanifest/#x_localized-members\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code class=\"notranslate\">*_localized</code> members</a>, aka localizable web app manifests. See <a href=\"https://chromestatus.com/feature/5090807862394880\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://chromestatus.com/feature/5090807862394880</a>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This PR adds a general data point for localizable members, plus specific data points for the <code class=\"notranslate\">dir</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">lang</code> manifest members, which I'm pretty sure were added at the same time (I've pinged engineering to check this) .</p>\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/29945",
